{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban ICBs from imposing minimum waiting periods for ADHD and autism assessments ",
        "additional_details": "We are calling on the Government to introduce national safeguards to protect meaningful patient choice and timely access to NHS-funded Right to Choose autism and ADHD assessments.\r\n \r\nPatients in England have a legal right to choose a healthcare provider for an ADHD or autism assessment yet some ICBs enforce minimum waits even when providers have capacity. Those unable to pay privately lose out most. We ask the government to protect patient choice by establishing national safeguards.\r\n",
        "background": "Introduce a ban on Integrated Care Boards (ICBs) imposing blanket minimum waiting periods where an eligible provider has assessment capacity.\r\n",
